source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Jira reads a link's visible text with no forced-newline rule at all: neither pair breaks, not even the last run of a token. jiro keeps every backslash in the link text.
-- input.jira --
[a\\b c\\d|http://x]
-- rendered.html --
<p><a href="http://x" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">a\\b c\\d</a></p>
-- want.md --
[a\\\\b c\\\\d](http://x)
-- warnings.json --
[]
